    "body": "### Problem\n\nRef: https://github.com/vim/vim/issues/20950\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* Create two files, one empty and another with two lines \"1\" and \"2\":\nprintf \"\" > temp1.txt\nprintf \"1\\n2\\n\" > temp2.txt\n\n* Then open vim in diff mode:\nnvim -u NONE -d temp1.txt temp2.txt\nIn the empty buffer temp1.txt type:\n\ndo\nu\n\ndo makes the buffers identical (correct)\nu (undo) leaves a residual last line \"2\" in temp1.txt (wrong).\n\n* The issue is reproduced with any number of lines, with undo always leaving the residual last line. Reproduced in nvim nightly and vim 9.2, indicating it is present in the common diff code.\n\n* The problem is not related to diff display. Even if :diffoff is executed after do, u still leaves the final line behind.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAfter :undo or normal u, the buffer should be restored to its original empty state.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1231+g2e3785a702\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nYes, Vim 9.2.390 behaves identically\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora 44\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nXTerm(406)\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\ndownloaded development release tarball for linux x86_64",
